From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Flax <hmccanne@exclamationpoint.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ipv6: addrconf: regenerate EUI-64 link-local on MAC change

addrconf_notify() handles NETDEV_UP/NETDEV_CHANGE (generate the link-local
when the carrier becomes ready) but has no NETDEV_CHANGEADDR case, so a
hardware address change after autoconfiguration has run never refreshes the
link-local.

On TiogaPass this matters: the ftgmac100 NCSI interface registers eth0 with a
u-boot placeholder MAC, the EUI-64 link-local is generated from it at
carrier-up, and only later does the NCSI OEM Get-MAC command replace dev_addr
with the NIC's real MAC (via dev_set_mac_address(), which emits
NETDEV_CHANGEADDR).  The link-local stays derived from the stale placeholder
MAC for the life of the interface.

Handle NETDEV_CHANGEADDR by rebuilding the autoconfigured addresses from the
new MAC, reusing the proven down/up cycle that the disable_ipv6 toggle uses
(dev_disable_change()).  Restricted to EUI-64 generation mode -- the only mode
whose link-local depends on the MAC -- and to an up, link-ready interface, so
statically configured and non-autoconf interfaces are untouched.

Signed-off-by: Flax <hmccanne@exclamationpoint.com>
---
diff --git a/net/ipv6/addrconf.c b/net/ipv6/addrconf.c
index a9358c796a81..3e7ba3ea31ab 100644
--- a/net/ipv6/addrconf.c
+++ b/net/ipv6/addrconf.c
@@ -3732,6 +3732,32 @@ static int addrconf_notify(struct notifier_block *this, unsigned long event,
 		addrconf_ifdown(dev, event != NETDEV_DOWN);
 		break;
 
+	case NETDEV_CHANGEADDR:
+		/* The hardware address changed after stateless autoconfiguration
+		 * already ran.  This happens with NC-SI: ftgmac100 registers the
+		 * interface with a bootloader placeholder MAC, the EUI-64
+		 * link-local is generated from it when the carrier first comes
+		 * up, and only later does the NCSI OEM Get-MAC command replace
+		 * dev_addr with the NIC's real MAC via dev_set_mac_address()
+		 * (which emits this event).  addrconf has no other path that
+		 * refreshes the link-local, so it stays derived from the stale
+		 * MAC.  Rebuild the autoconfigured addresses from the new MAC by
+		 * cycling IPv6 down then up, exactly as the disable_ipv6 toggle
+		 * does (see dev_disable_change()).  Restricted to EUI-64 mode --
+		 * the only address generation mode whose link-local depends on
+		 * the MAC -- and to a link that is up and ready, so that
+		 * statically configured and non-autoconf interfaces are left
+		 * untouched.
+		 */
+		if (!IS_ERR_OR_NULL(idev) && !idev->cnf.disable_ipv6 &&
+		    !(dev->priv_flags & IFF_NO_ADDRCONF) &&
+		    idev->cnf.addr_gen_mode == IN6_ADDR_GEN_MODE_EUI64 &&
+		    netif_running(dev) && addrconf_link_ready(dev)) {
+			addrconf_notify(this, NETDEV_DOWN, ptr);
+			addrconf_notify(this, NETDEV_UP, ptr);
+		}
+		break;
+
 	case NETDEV_CHANGENAME:
 		if (idev) {
 			snmp6_unregister_dev(idev);
